apps/driver/modules/capture-native/android/.gradle/

# PSP vendor material: the protocol guide is CONFIDENTIAL-footered on all 80 pages and
# apitoken.txt is a live credential. Neither may enter git history (Q-H1, 2026-08-19).
docs/psp-docs/

# Scratch worktrees created by Claude Code — a full stale copy of the app. Only .git/info/exclude
# listed it, which is local-to-one-clone; this makes every clone ignore it.
#
# ⚠ It does NOT stop Tailwind scanning it. Verified 2026-08-23: after every source using z-[9998],
# z-[9999] and z-[10000] was gone, those utilities were still emitted into the local bundle, and
# neither this entry, nor `@source not`, nor clearing node_modules/.vite changed the output byte.
# The pollution is local-only — CI and Railway check out without this directory — but it means a
# local `vite build` is NOT a faithful check of what ships, and dead CSS inflates it. Same root
# cause as the ~700 phantom eslint errors. Unresolved; do not trust local bundle contents alone.
.claude/worktrees/

# Carrier TMS inspection notes and credentials (McLeod / LoadMaster).
#
# `setup.md` carries a live SQL Server login, and the rest of the directory is a complete schema map
# of a CUSTOMER's production system — internal host address included. This repository is PUBLIC, and
# between 2026-08-21 and 2026-08-24 that credential was readable by anyone on origin/main (commits
# a286370, 985b698). It was untracked once already (41ab398) and came back on a later merge, which is
# exactly why this entry exists rather than a one-off `git rm --cached`.
#
# Untracking does NOT remove the credential from history — rotation is the mitigation, this entry only
# stops it recurring. Same posture as docs/psp-docs/ above.
docs/McLeod-Testing/

# The McLeod agent's sync state (tools/mcleod-agent/agent.mjs — STATE_PATH, ROSTER_STATE_PATH).
#
# The VALUES in roster-state.json are row hashes and harmless. The KEYS are not: 164 driver codes
# (ABRAVO, ACASTILL — a carrier's actual driver identifiers), 190 unit numbers and 235 trailer
# numbers. This repository is PUBLIC. Committing it would publish a customer's roster — the same
# class of mistake as the McLeod credentials above, caught before it happened rather than after.
#
# Both defaults now resolve beside agent.mjs rather than to the CWD, so `tools/mcleod-agent/` is
# where they land however the agent is invoked. The bare names stay because they are what four days
# of running it from the repository root already produced, and because an operator who sets
# STATE_PATH by hand will reach for the old relative path.
tools/mcleod-agent/state.json
tools/mcleod-agent/roster-state.json
roster-state.json
state.json

# Playwright MCP scratch (snapshots, console logs, screenshots) — written into whatever directory the
# server is started from, which is the repository root.
.playwright-mcp/
